<mxCell id="c49" value="7" style="ellipse;html=1;fillColor=#0972D3;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;aspect=fixed;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="580" y="730" width="22" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="c50" value="1) Checkout calls POST /orders with an Idempotency-Key.   2) One conditional write stores the order; the stream is the outbox.   3) Pipes turns status changes into events on the bus.&lt;br&gt;4) Rules fan out to queues, never straight to fragile code.   5) The saga orchestrates stock, fraud, warehouse and capture, with compensations.   6) Max concurrency 20 protects the warehouse API.   7) ERP gets changes in order, per order." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#3C4043;fontStyle=0;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="924" width="1440" height="34" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
</mxfile>
